Tool Purpose <code>create_upload_url()</code> Single-use upload link, valid 10 minutes, for one file up to the hub limit (200 MiB) → <code>{upload_url, token_header, token, expires_at, max_bytes, curl}</code>. The agent runs <code>curl</code> in its shell with the file path filled in and gets <code>{upload_id, sha256, size}</code>. The file's bytes go straight to the hub and never pass through the model. <code>upload_content(filename, content_base64, sha256)</code> Upload a tiny file inline (at most 8 MiB decoded) → <code>{upload_id, sha256, size}</code>. <code>sha256</code> is the hex digest of the original file; if the decoded content does not match it, nothing is uploaded. Models copy long base64 strings unreliably, so prefer <code>create_upload_url</code> for anything but a few KB. <code>transcribe_audio(upload_id \| path, execution_profile?, language?, profile?, instructions?, options?, diarize?, private=true, idempotency_key?)</code> Submit an audio job → <code>{job_id, status, private}</code> immediately. <code>options</code>: <code>translate</code>, <code>word_timestamps</code>, <code>vad_filter</code>, <code>diarize</code>. <code>diarize=true</code> (same as <code>options.diarize</code>) labels who spoke when: the result's segments carry a 1-based <code>speaker</code> number and the Markdown starts each speaker section with <code>**Sprecher N:**</code> (language <code>de</code>) or <code>**Speaker N:**</code>; only a worker with a verified diarizer takes the job, until then it stays <code>pending</code> (<code>no_capable_worker</code>). Omitted, the execution profile's <code>diarize</code> setting applies (default off); <code>diarize=false</code> turns it off. <code>instructions</code> (also on <code>convert_document</code> and <code>postprocess_text</code>): user instructions for the profile's LLM steps, sent as the user message while the profile prompt stays the system message; needs a profile with an <code>llm</code>/<code>extract</code> step (else hub <code>422 invalid_instructions</code>). <code>convert_document(upload_id \| path, …, options?)</code> Submit a PDF/image/Word DOCX → Markdown job → <code>{job_id, status, private}</code>. <code>options</code>: <code>languages</code> (<code>de</code>, <code>en</code>, <code>fr</code>, <code>it</code>, <code>es</code>, <code>ko</code>), <code>ocr</code>, <code>ocr_engine</code>, <code>page_start</code>, <code>page_end</code>, <code>pipeline</code>, <code>image_scale</code> (1.0–4.0, OCR raster multiplier), <code>ocr_min_confidence</code> (0–1, <code>rapidocr</code> only), <code>remove_repeated_headers</code> (drop letterheads and footers repeated on most pages); a DOCX takes none of the OCR/page options; see the API reference. <code>postprocess_text(upload_id \| path \| job_id, profile, instructions?, language?, private=true, idempotency_key?)</code> Run a stored postprocess profile on text, no engine (a <code>text</code> job) → <code>{job_id, status, private}</code> immediately. <code>profile</code> is required (missing → tool error <code>profile_required</code>, nothing is sent). <code>upload_id</code>/<code>path</code> name a UTF-8 text or Markdown file (hub text cap <code>RESONA_MAX_TEXT_UPLOAD_BYTES</code>, default 2 MiB). <code>job_id</code> re-runs a profile on an earlier completed job's result without re-transcribing: the tool reads that result in hub range reads of at most 32 768 characters (<code>GET /v1/jobs/{id}/result/markdown?source=raw</code>, so the unpolished <code>raw_markdown</code> when the result has one, else <code>markdown</code>), uploads it as text and submits the job; <code>language</code> defaults to the earlier job's. A result over 2 MiB (the hub's default text cap) fails as soon as <code>total_chars</code> or the bytes read exceed it; hub errors on the source job (<code>404 not_found</code>, <code>409 not_ready</code>, <code>410 result_expired</code>) become tool errors and nothing is uploaded; a hub without <code>source=raw</code> support is refused rather than re-polishing the polished text. With <code>job_id</code>, <code>private=false</code> is refused when the source job is private, so a private transcript never reaches non-private processing through this tool. Read the output with <code>get_job</code> / <code>get_result</code> as for any job. <code>get_job(job_id)</code> Status (<code>pending</code> with <code>queue_reason</code>, <code>processing</code>, <code>completed</code>, <code>failed</code>, <code>cancelled</code>). <code>get_result(job_id, offset=0, limit=32768)</code> One Markdown chunk plus <code>next_offset</code>, <code>total_chars</code>, language, warnings, provenance. Each call is one hub range read (<code>GET /v1/jobs/{id}/result/markdown</code>), so the full result never passes through the MCP server. Concatenating chunks from offset 0 until <code>next_offset</code> is <code>null</code> reproduces the REST <code>markdown</code> exactly. <code>limit</code> is capped at 32 768 characters. <code>cancel_job(job_id)</code> Request cancellation; later worker output is rejected. <code>list_engines()</code> The organization's execution profiles (approved engine/model/accelerator candidates) and the engines it can use now (<code>GET /v1/engines</code>: tuples that an approved worker of the organization has tested; cloud providers only when cloud processing is enabled). <code>get_settings()</code> The organization's current non-secret settings revision (read-only). <p>There are no tools that change settings or profiles, issue or revoke credentials, or enroll workers. Use <code>resona settings</code> and <code>resona-admin</code> for those.</p> <p>Speaker diarization (<code>diarize=true</code>) has limits: speakers can be merged on short recordings with several voices, at most 8 speakers, and engines without word timestamps split speakers only at segment boundaries. See CLI guide: Limits.</p> <p>Jobs are private by default. <code>private=false</code> only works when the organization has enabled cloud processing; otherwise the hub answers <code>policy_denied</code>. There is no fallback to another provider or to local processing.</p> <p>A typical agent flow:</p> <pre><code>create_upload_url()                            → {curl: "curl … -F 'file=@&lt;PATH&gt;' …"}
$ curl … -F 'file=@memo.wav' …                 → {upload_id}
transcribe_audio(upload_id=…)                  → {job_id: 12, status: "pending", private: true}
get_job(12)                                    → … status: "completed"
get_result(12)                                 → {markdown: "...", next_offset: 32768, total_chars: 51234}
get_result(12, offset=32768)                   → … until next_offset is null
</code></pre> <p>Re-polishing an earlier transcript with another stored profile:</p> <pre><code>postprocess_text(job_id=12, profile="transcript-polish-de")  → {job_id: 13, status: "pending", private: true}
get_job(13) … get_result(13)
</code></pre>
